  <section id="s-indexshare" data-code="indexshare">
    <div class="section-no">03 — IndexShare Attention</div>
    <h2>IndexShare: Scaling Context to 1 Million Tokens</h2>
    <p>To process code repositories, GLM-5.2 extends the context window to 1 million tokens. However, standard attention scales quadratically $O(L^2)$ with sequence length, making long context processing slow and expensive. DeepSeek Sparse Attention (DSA) optimizes this by using an <strong>Indexer</strong> that computes token relevance scores and restricts attention calculations to only the top-$k$ ($k=2048$) most important tokens, saving 1.5–2× compute.</p>
    <p>But at a 1-million-token context length, even computing the indexer for every attention layer becomes a significant computational bottleneck. GLM-5.2 introduces <strong>IndexShare</strong> to solve this. Because token relevance changes slowly across adjacent layers, IndexShare reuses the same indexer routing decision across blocks of four layers. Only Layer 1 (and Layer 5, 9, etc.) computes the sparse indexer, while the next three layers load the indexer results from a cached list. This reduces per-token attention FLOPs by <strong>2.9×</strong> at 1M context length with zero loss in retrieval accuracy.</p>
    
