  <section id="s-distillation" data-code="distillation">
    <div class="section-no">06 — Distill & Benchmarks</div>
    <h2>Cross-Stage Distillation & Real-World PAYOFF</h2>
    <p>GLM-5 is aligned via a sequential RL pipeline: first <strong>Reasoning RL</strong> (math, code, science reasoning), followed by <strong>Agentic RL</strong> (SWE-bench, terminal tasks, multi-hop search), and concluding with <strong>General RL</strong> (human alignment). However, optimizing sequentially causes models to forget previously learned skills (catastrophic forgetting). To solve this, Zhipu AI uses <strong>On-Policy Cross-Stage Distillation</strong>. The checkpoints from SFT and preceding RL stages act as "teacher" models. During training, advantage values are calculated directly as the relative log-ratio between the current policy and the teacher models, allowing the model to quickly recover previously learned skills.</p>
    <p>Through these optimizations, GLM-5 achieves state-of-the-art results on agentic, coding, and long-horizon reasoning benchmarks, surpassing both open and closed models on complex tasks.</p>
    
